  "result": "All three fixes are applied:\n\n1. `src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts` — `updateEndpoint` now checks `input.enabled === undefined` instead of the truthy-only `input.enabled &&`, so setting `enabled: false` actually persists.\n2. `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts` — the delivery job now marks a claimed delivery failed when its endpoint is disabled (in addition to the existing \"endpoint no longer exists\" case), instead of delivering it.\n3. `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts` — `createWebhook`'s quota check now counts all endpoints (`live.length`) instead of only enabled ones, so disabling an endpoint no longer frees up a slot.",
